Commercial Services Group is undertaking Preliminary Market Engagement (PME) to explore options for the future delivery of its end-to-end recruitment technology service. This is not currently a tender or invitation to bid. The purpose is to understand what the market can offer before deciding whether to retain and improve the existing solution or procure an alternative.
The requirement covers a Recruitment CRM and Applicant Tracking System (ATS) together with compliance, onboarding, worker management, timesheets, payroll inputs/pay processing support, billing, invoicing, financial controls and reporting. It must also support candidate and client portals and integrations with recruitment websites, job boards, Microsoft 365, telephony, messaging, finance and payroll systems.
The solution needs to operate across 10 separate recruitment joint ventures, alongside a central back-office function and finance teams. The JVs are separate legal entities, so the system must enable shared working while maintaining appropriate separation of candidate, worker, client, commercial and financial data.
CSG is deliberately not prescribing a particular technology solution. Suppliers can propose a single integrated platform, a modular solution, specialist components or an alternative operating model, provided they can demonstrate clear ownership, integration, accountability and value.
The PME is particularly seeking to understand:
what functionality is available as standard, configurable, bespoke, third-party or roadmap capability;
implementation, data migration and integration approaches;
licensing and commercial models, including how costs scale as JVs, users and transaction volumes change;
opportunities to simplify the current approach;
implementation and operational risks;
appropriate use of automation and AI;
indicative implementation, recurring and whole-life costs.
Indicative scale includes approximately 156 central/JV users, 6,000+ candidates, 1,200–1,500 active contingent workers per month, around 29,000 placements and 167,600+ timesheets annually.
In simple terms: CSG is testing the market for a modern replacement or improvement to the technology that runs the entire recruitment operation from candidate attraction through compliance and placement to timesheets, pay, billing and reporting, before determining its final procurement strategy.

