The Authority is undertaking preliminary market engagement in relation to the potential future supply and through-life support of Fixed and Portable Atmosphere Monitoring Systems (AMS) and associated equipment and services.
The potential requirement may include, but is not limited to:
- supply of AMS equipment, approved replacements, spares, consumables, accessories and associated support equipment;
- inspection, maintenance, calibration, survey, repair and refurbishment of in-scope equipment;
- technical support, fault investigation, defect resolution and reliability improvement;
- logistics, inventory and supply-chain support;
- technical documentation and configuration management;
- software and firmware support;
- obsolescence management, including identification and implementation of suitable replacement solutions;
- training and associated support;
- mobilisation, transition and knowledge transfer; and
- performance management and reporting.
The purpose of this market engagement is to help the Authority understand market capability, capacity and appetite, and to obtain information that may assist in developing the requirement and informing the future procurement and commercial strategy.
The scope, procurement route, commercial model, contract structure, duration, estimated value and delivery arrangements have not yet been determined and may be subject to change. Any subsequent procurement opportunity will be advertised separately through the appropriate procurement notice.
This notice is published for preliminary market engagement and information-gathering purposes only. It does not constitute a call for competition, invitation to tender, pre-qualification exercise, request for expressions of interest, offer or commitment by the Ministry of Defence to undertake a procurement or place a contract.
Interested organisations should refer to the Atmosphere Monitoring Systems Request for Information (RFI) for further information and instructions on how to participate in the market engagement. - https://contracts.mod.uk/esop/guest/go/opportunity/detail?opportunityId=61704

Mentimeter turns presentations into conversations and allows improved learning outcomes and increases student satisfaction.  Mentimeter focuses on online collaboration:
It allows users: 
To easily facilitate active learning and give them power to participate;
Run real-time formative assessments that check knowledge and understanding;
Collect ideas, opinions, and instant feedback to foster student-centered learning;
Modernize teaching with the same experience for in-person and online students.

NHS Blood and Transplant (NHSBT) is undertaking preliminary market engagement in relation to a potential procurement for an enterprise-wide Digital Archiving & Storage Solution and associated services.
NHSBT is seeking to understand the market's capability to provide a secure, scalable and governed approach to the long-term retention, management, preservation, discovery and retrieval of digital information across the organisation.
The anticipated scope may include:
provision of an enterprise Digital Archiving & Storage platform;
discovery, implementation, configuration and deployment;
migration and onboarding of structured and unstructured data from existing applications, storage locations and legacy repositories;
long-term digital preservation capabilities;
information governance, retention, legal hold and controlled disposal;
search, retrieval, export and audit capabilities;
integration with NHSBT's existing technology estate;
professional and advisory services covering archive strategy, information lifecycle management, records management and operating model development;
service management, support and maintenance;
training and knowledge transfer; and
exit, data portability and transition services.
NHSBT's current requirement anticipates the solution supporting business, corporate and operational functions across the organisation. The procurement is intended to reduce risks associated with unmanaged data growth, legacy storage approaches and inconsistent retention practices while supporting information governance, security, regulatory compliance and future digital transformation.

